<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Illinois."><title>Illinois Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Illinois</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Illinois</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>211 Illinois</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Illinois phone, or text your zip code to 898211, for free, confidential help finding local assistance: housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and mental health. As of 2026, 211 covers all 102 Illinois counties around the clock.</p><div><a href="/programs/211-illinois/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/211-illinois/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Illinois Legal Aid Online (Eviction &amp; Legal Help)</h3><p>Free, plain-language legal information for Illinoisans, guided court-form tools, and a directory to find a local legal aid provider. Illinois Legal Aid Online covers eviction, benefits, family law, debt, and more.</p><div><a href="/programs/illinois-legal-aid-online-eviction-and-legal-help/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/illinois-legal-aid-online-eviction-and-legal-help/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>All Kids (Illinois Children&#39;s Health Coverage)</h3><p>All Kids is Illinois&#39; health coverage for children, covering doctor visits, dental, vision, and more. Many families pay no premiums or co-payments. Apply online, on paper, or with help from a partner; the All Kids Hotline is 1-866-255-5437.</p><div><a href="/programs/all-kids-illinois-childrens-health-coverage/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/all-kids-illinois-childrens-health-coverage/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Medicaid (Illinois HFS)</h3><p>Illinois Medicaid is free or low-cost health coverage run by the Department of Healthcare and Family Services. Adults 19 to 64 can qualify with income up to 138 percent of the federal poverty level under the ACA Adult category. Apply online at ABE (abe.illinois.gov), by phone at the DHS Help Line 1-800-843-6154, or at a Family Community Resource Center.</p><div><a href="/programs/medicaid-illinois-hfs/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/medicaid-illinois-hfs/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Home Weatherization Assistance Program (Illinois DCEO)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible Illinoisans: air sealing, insulation, and heating-system repairs that lower future bills. Run through Community Action Agencies and overseen by the Department of Commerce and Economic Opportunity. The Help Illinois Families call center is 1-833-711-0374.</p><div><a href="/programs/home-weatherization-assistance-program-illinois-dceo/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/home-weatherization-assistance-program-illinois-dceo/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>LIHEAP Energy Assistance (Illinois)</h3><p>Illinois LIHEAP helps low-income households pay heating and cooling bills, with priority help for emergencies. Apply during your assignment month at helpillinoisfamilies.com or through a local Community Action Agency; the Help Illinois Families hotline is 1-833-711-0374. For the 2025-2026 program year, applications run from fall 2025 through August 15, 2026, or until funding runs out.</p><div><a href="/programs/liheap-energy-assistance-illinois/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/liheap-energy-assistance-illinois/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Illinois Earned Income Credit</h3><p>Illinois&#39; state Earned Income Credit is a refundable tax credit worth 20 percent of your federal Earned Income Tax Credit. If you qualify for the federal EITC, you qualify for the Illinois credit. Claim it on your Illinois state return; free tax-prep sites can file it.</p><div><a href="/programs/illinois-earned-income-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/illinois-earned-income-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Illinois WIC</h3><p>Healthy food on a WIC EBT card, nutrition education, and breastfeeding support for pregnant and new mothers, infants, and children under 5. Find your local office through the DHS Office Locator and make an appointment; the State WIC Office is 1-844-901-0962.</p><div><a href="/programs/illinois-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/illinois-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>SNAP Food Stamps (Illinois)</h3><p>Illinois SNAP loads monthly food money on the Illinois Link card, which works like a debit card at grocery stores. Apply online at ABE (abe.illinois.gov), by phone, or at your local Family Community Resource Center. The DHS Help Line is 1-800-843-6154.</p><div><a href="/programs/snap-food-stamps-illinois/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/snap-food-stamps-illinois/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>TANF Cash Assistance (Illinois)</h3><p>Illinois TANF pays monthly cash to pregnant people and families with children, loaded on the Illinois Link card. Adults are limited to 60 months of cash assistance in a lifetime. Apply online at ABE (abe.illinois.gov) or at your local Family Community Resource Center; the DHS Help Line is 1-800-843-6154.</p><div><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-assistance-illinois/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-assistance-illinois/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (Illinois IDES)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from the Illinois Department of Employment Security. File your claim online, or call IDES Claimant Services at 1-800-244-5631. Certify for each week you claim through the automated Tele-Serve line at 1-312-338-4337.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-illinois-ides/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-illinois-ides/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>